{"name":"Hibiscus Delight","hex":"#fe9773","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hibiscus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flowering plant of the genus Hibiscus, especially Hibiscus syriacus, found in tropical to temperate regions, of some species used for making infusions/tea.","A cocktail made with champagne and cranberry juice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hibiscus"},{"term":"delight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Joy; pleasure.","Something that gives great joy or pleasure."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To give delight to; to affect with great pleasure; to please highly.","To have or take great pleasure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hibiscus","blocks":[{"text":"Hibiscus is a genus of plants in the family Malvaceae native to the tropics and subtropics. The genus is quite large, comprising 319 species. Hibiscus are renowned for their large, showy flowers and those species are commonly known simply as \"hibiscus\", or less widely known as rose mallow. The genus includes both annual and perennial herbaceous plants, as well as woody shrubs and small trees."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Hibiscus_flower_TZ.jpg/330px-Hibiscus_flower_TZ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hibiscus","wikidata":"Q157124"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg/500px-Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg/1280px-Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wi